---
name: web_presentation_maker
description: Generates standalone 16:9 HTML presentation decks with responsive auto-scaling, slide navigation, keyboard shortcuts, print/PDF layout support, helper modal, image search recommendations, and Google Drive upload delivery. Use when the user asks to create an HTML presentation, web slide deck, presentation web page, or HTML 교안.
---

# Web Presentation Maker Skill

Generates professional, standalone 16:9 single-file HTML presentation decks with built-in slide navigation, responsive auto-scaling, print/PDF support, and shortcut help modal UI. Uploads/delivers the HTML presentation and provides a structured slide-by-slide Image Search & Rename Guide.

## When to Use

- Creating web-based slide decks, HTML 교안, or interactive presentations in a single HTML file.
- Converting text drafts, outlines, or lecture content into structured presentation slides.
- Designing responsive, interactive 16:9 slides with print/PDF export support.

---

## Key Features & Specifications

### 1. Single-file Deck Structure
All HTML structure, CSS styling, and Vanilla JavaScript interactive logic MUST be self-contained in a single `.html` document without external JavaScript runtime dependencies.

### 2. 16:9 Responsive Auto-scaling
- Fixed `.deck` container canvas sized at `1280px` x `720px`.
- Centered on screen with flexible dynamic CSS scaling using `transform: scale(s)` where:
  $$\text{scale } s = \min\left(\frac{\text{window.innerWidth}}{1280}, \frac{\text{window.innerHeight}}{720}\right)$$
- Automatically recalculates on window `resize` events.

### 3. Navigation Engine
- Active slide switching managed via JavaScript `goTo(index)` function.
- CSS transitions for smooth sliding fade effects (`translateX` and `opacity`).
- Multi-input support:
  - **Keyboard**: `ArrowRight`, `ArrowLeft`, `Space`, `PageDown`, `PageUp`, `Home`, `End`.
  - **Mouse**: Invisible left/right click hover zones (`.nav-zone.left`, `.nav-zone.right`).
  - **Mobile Touch**: Touch swipe distance detection (`touchstart`, `touchend`).

### 4. Floating UI Controls & Helper Modal
- Bottom progress bar (`#progressBar`) showing completion percentage.
- Bottom-right page indicator (`#pageIndicator`, e.g., `1 / 5`).
- Bottom-right help button (`.help-btn` with `?` icon) opening a popup modal (`#helpModal`).
- Modal trigger shortcuts: `?` or `H` key to open/close, `Esc` to close.
- Modal content displays all available keyboard controls:
  - `F`: Fullscreen toggle
  - `O`: Slide overview grid
  - `P`: Print / Save as PDF
  - `Esc`: Close overlay

### 5. User-Provided Image & Ultra-Simple Number Mapping Policy
To streamline image collection and local rendering:
- **Slide-by-Slide Search Queries**: For every slide containing an image frame, generate tailored **Search Queries (추천 검색어 - 한글 & 영문)** in the response guide so the user can easily find optimal photos on Google Images or stock sites.
- **Ultra-Simple Single-Digit File Naming**: Images are mapped by plain slide numbers (`1.jpg`, `2.jpg`, `3.jpg`, etc.). When Windows hides extensions, typing `1` (or `1.jpg`) is fully supported.
- **Robust Path & Windows Double-Extension Fallback in HTML**: All HTML `<img>` tags MUST include automatic JS `onerror` fallbacks to support direct root directory placement, subfolder placement (`images/1.jpg` or `img/1.jpg`), `.jpg` / `.png` variations, and Windows double-extension (`1.jpg.jpg`):
  ```html
  <img src="1.jpg" onerror="if(!this.t1){this.t1=true;this.src='1.jpg.jpg';}else if(!this.t2){this.t2=true;this.src='images/1.jpg';}else if(!this.t3){this.t3=true;this.src='images/1.jpg.jpg';}else if(!this.t4){this.t4=true;this.src='img/1.jpg';}else if(!this.t5){this.t5=true;this.src='1.png';}else if(!this.t6){this.t6=true;this.src='1.png.png';}else if(!this.t7){this.t7=true;this.src='images/1.png';}" alt="Slide 1 Image">
  ```

### 6. Print & PDF Layout (`@media print`)
- Hides interactive floating UI overlays (`.progress-bar`, `.page-indicator`, `.nav-zone`, `.help-btn`, `.help-modal`).
- Disables `transform: scale()` and forces `page-break-after: always` per slide for standard 16:9 landscape printing.

---

## Slide Component Palette

- **Title Slide**: `.title-kicker`, `.title-main`, `.title-sub`, `.title-tags`.
- **Comparison Block**: `.fail-row` with `.fail-col.bad` and `.fail-col.good`.
- **KPI Metrics Row**: `.kpi-row` with `.kpi` cards.
- **Image Gallery & Frame**: `.gal` with `.img-frame` (real image or user placeholder).
- **Hero Grid**: `.tfhero` with `.fimg` image/frame and `.fside` content column.
- **Callout Notes**: `.info-block` and `.ai-note` with `gold`, `warn`, or default theme accents.
- **Summary Table**: `.summary-table` for key structured data.

---

## Standard Single-File HTML Template Code

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="ko">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Presentation Title</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Pretendard:wght@300;400;600;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #0d0f17;
      --card-bg: #161926;
      --text-main: #f0f4fc;
      --text-sub: #94a3b8;
      --purple: #8b5cf6;
      --gold: #f59e0b;
      --rust: #ef4444;
      --green: #10b981;
      --accent: #3b82f6;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    body {
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text-main);
      font-family: 'Pretendard', sans-serif;
      overflow: hidden;
      width: 100vw;
      height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .deck-container {
      width: 1280px;
      height: 720px;
      position: relative;
      transform-origin: center center;
    }
    .slide {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0; left: 0;
      width: 1280px;
      height: 720px;
      background: var(--card-bg);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 60px 80px;
      opacity: 0;
      visibility: hidden;
      transform: translateX(40px);
      transition: all 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: space-between;
      overflow: hidden;
      box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
    }
    .slide.active {
      opacity: 1;
      visibility: visible;
      transform: translateX(0);
    }

    /* Floating Controls */
    .progress-bar {
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 0; left: 0; height: 5px;
      background: var(--purple);
      transition: width 0.3s ease;
      z-index: 100;
    }
    .page-indicator {
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 20px; right: 20px;
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
      backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
      padding: 6px 14px;
      border-radius: 20px;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--text-sub);
      z-index: 100;
    }
    .nav-zone {
      position: fixed; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 15%;
      z-index: 90; cursor: pointer;
    }
    .nav-zone.left { left: 0; }
    .nav-zone.right { right: 0; }
    .help-btn {
      position: fixed; bottom: 20px; right: 80px;
      width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); border: none;
      color: white; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;
      z-index: 100; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    }
    .help-modal {
      display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0;
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.8); backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
      z-index: 200; justify-content: center; align-items: center;
    }
    .help-modal.active { display: flex; }
    .help-content {
      background: var(--card-bg); padding: 40px; border-radius: 16px;
      max-width: 500px; width: 90%; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
    }

    /* Print Styles */
    @media print {
      body { overflow: visible; background: #fff; color: #000; }
      .deck-container { transform: none !important; width: 100%; height: auto; }
      .slide {
        position: relative !important;
        opacity: 1 !important;
        visibility: visible !important;
        transform: none !important;
        page-break-after: always;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        box-shadow: none;
        border: 1px solid #ccc;
      }
      .progress-bar, .page-indicator, .nav-zone, .help-btn, .help-modal { display: none !important; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="deck-container" id="deckContainer">
    <!-- Slide 1 -->
    <div class="slide active">
      <div class="title-kicker">PRESENTATION TITLE</div>
      <h1 class="title-main">메인 슬라이드 제목</h1>
      <p class="title-sub">부제목 및 간단한 설명 문구</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Slide 2 with Image Fallback Example -->
    <div class="slide">
      <h2>이미지 포함 슬라이드</h2>
      <img src="1.jpg" onerror="if(!this.t1){this.t1=true;this.src='1.jpg.jpg';}else if(!this.t2){this.t2=true;this.src='images/1.jpg';}else if(!this.t3){this.t3=true;this.src='images/1.jpg.jpg';}else if(!this.t4){this.t4=true;this.src='img/1.jpg';}else if(!this.t5){this.t5=true;this.src='1.png';}else if(!this.t6){this.t6=true;this.src='1.png.png';}else if(!this.t7){this.t7=true;this.src='images/1.png';}" alt="Slide 1 Image" style="max-width: 100%; border-radius: 8px;">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="progress-bar" id="progressBar"></div>
  <div class="page-indicator" id="pageIndicator">1 / 2</div>
  <div class="nav-zone left" onclick="prevSlide()"></div>
  <div class="nav-zone right" onclick="nextSlide()"></div>
  <button class="help-btn" onclick="toggleHelp()">?</button>

  <div class="help-modal" id="helpModal" onclick="toggleHelp()">
    <div class="help-content" onclick="event.stopPropagation()">
      <h3>단축키 안내</h3>
      <ul style="margin-top: 15px; line-height: 1.8;">
        <li><b>→ / Space / PageDown</b> : 다음 슬라이드</li>
        <li><b>← / PageUp</b> : 이전 슬라이드</li>
        <li><b>Home / End</b> : 처음 / 마지막 슬라이드</li>
        <li><b>F</b> : 전체화면 토글</li>
        <li><b>P</b> : 인쇄 및 PDF 저장</li>
        <li><b>? / H</b> : 단축키 도움말 토글</li>
        <li><b>Esc</b> : 닫기</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    const slides = document.querySelectorAll('.slide');
    const total = slides.length;
    let current = 0;

    function scaleDeck() {
      const container = document.getElementById('deckContainer');
      const scale = Math.min(window.innerWidth / 1280, window.innerHeight / 720);
      container.style.transform = `scale(${scale})`;
    }
    window.addEventListener('resize', scaleDeck);
    scaleDeck();

    function goTo(index) {
      if (index < 0) index = 0;
      if (index >= total) index = total - 1;
      slides[current].classList.remove('active');
      current = index;
      slides[current].classList.add('active');
      document.getElementById('progressBar').style.width = `${((current + 1) / total) * 100}%`;
      document.getElementById('pageIndicator').innerText = `${current + 1} / ${total}`;
    }

    function nextSlide() { goTo(current + 1); }
    function prevSlide() { goTo(current - 1); }

    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key === 'ArrowRight' || e.key === ' ' || e.key === 'PageDown') nextSlide();
      else if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft' || e.key === 'PageUp') prevSlide();
      else if (e.key === 'Home') goTo(0);
      else if (e.key === 'End') goTo(total - 1);
      else if (e.key === '?' || e.key.toLowerCase() === 'h') toggleHelp();
      else if (e.key.toLowerCase() === 'f') {
        if (!document.fullscreenElement) document.documentElement.requestFullscreen();
        else document.exitFullscreen();
      } else if (e.key.toLowerCase() === 'p') window.print();
      else if (e.key === 'Escape') document.getElementById('helpModal').classList.remove('active');
    });

    function toggleHelp() {
      document.getElementById('helpModal').classList.toggle('active');
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## Execution Workflow & Output Deliverables

1. **Extract Narrative Beats**: Parse the user's content into structured slides.
2. **Assign Layouts & Styling**: Build the full single-file HTML presentation.
3. **Save / Upload File**:
   - Save the file locally (e.g. `presentation.html`).
   - If Google Drive features are configured, upload via `drive:create_file` (base64 encoded) and return a clickable link (`webViewLink`).
4. **Deliver Image Search & Rename Guide**:
   In the final response to the user, include the following table format for image mapping:

   | 슬라이드 번호 | 이미지 용도 / 주제 | 추천 검색어 (한글 / 영문) | 저장할 파일명 (단순 숫자) |
   |:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
   | 1 | 메인 타이틀 배경 | 인공지능 미래 기술 / Futuristic AI Technology | `1` (또는 `1.jpg`, `images/1.jpg`) |
   | 3 | 서비스 비교 비주얼 | 데이터 분석 차트 / Data analytics dashboard | `3` (또는 `3.jpg`, `images/3.jpg`) |

---

